    "q-333064": {
      "dom_id": "step-q333064",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{2}(t)+4,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}} $,\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2s+4}{s(s-3)}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{3{x}_{2}(t)+4\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=3L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+4L\\{1\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1={X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2=3{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{4}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the second equation for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-2 & =3{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =2+\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+4}{s} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s+4}{s(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the first equation and solving for ${X}_{1}(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1 & ={X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =2{X}_{2}(s)-1 \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =2(\\frac{2s+4}{s(s-3)})-1 \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{4s+8}{s(s-3)}-1 \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{4s+8-s(s-3)}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{4s+8-{s}^{2}+3s}{s(s-3)} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+7s+8}{s(s-3)} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+7s+8}{s(s-1)(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{-{s}^{2}+7s+8}{s(s-1)(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2s+4}{s(s-3)}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
