    "q-333068": {
      "dom_id": "step-q333068",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{2}(t)+5,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}} $,\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{s+5}{s(s-2)}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{2}(t)+5\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}+5L\\{1\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2=3{X}_{1}(s)-{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-1=2{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{5}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the second equation for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-1 & =2{X}_{2}(s)+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =1+\\frac{5}{s} \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{s+5}{s} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{s+5}{s(s-2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the first equation and solving for ${X}_{1}(s)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2 & =3{X}_{1}(s)-{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =2-{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =2-(\\frac{s+5}{s(s-2)}) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2s(s-2)-(s+5)}{s(s-2)} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2({s}^{2}-2s)-s-5}{s(s-2)} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-4s-s-5}{s(s-2)} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-5s-5}{s(s-2)} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}-5s-5}{s(s-2)(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2{s}^{2}-5s-5}{s(s-2)(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{s+5}{s(s-2)}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
