    "q-330955": {
      "dom_id": "step-q330955",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+3 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3-2s}{s(s-1)},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)+3\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+3L\\{1\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+3L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+2={X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-1=-{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+2 & ={X}_{1}(s)+\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{3}{s}-2 \\\\ (s-1){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{3-2s}{s} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{3-2s}{s(s-1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)-1 & =-{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =1-{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =1-(\\frac{3-2s}{s(s-1)}) \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{s(s-1)-3+2s}{s(s-1)} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-s-3+2s}{s(s-1)} \\\\ (s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}+s-3}{s(s-1)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}+s-3}{s(s-1)(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system  in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3-2s}{s(s-1)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{{s}^{2}+s-3}{s(s-1)(s-3)}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
