      "source_example_id": "e-21577",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution",
      "kp_id": "e-21577"
    },
    "q-333133": {
      "dom_id": "step-q333133",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+9{x}_{2}(t)+9 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{2}(t)+2,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{3}{s-2},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{1}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"35px\" align=\"center\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"40px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{3}{s-2}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s+1}\\}+3\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{-1\\cdot t}+3{e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & ={e}^{-t}+3{e}^{2t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}-\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\}-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\cdot t}-1 \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{2t}+{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}-1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
